  "extra_findings": [
    "Visibility rule not enforced in the listing (index.php:73, F3) and in the CSV export (index.php:44-47, F4) — same class as SEC-017 at other points; fixed via listarChamadosVisiveis/exportarCsvVisivel while the public listarChamados/exportarCsv keep returning everything (rule 6 enforcement, not COMP)",
    "Race condition on the fixed shared export file EXPORT_DIR/chamados.csv (lib.php:125-150, F8) — concurrent exports truncate each other; fixed by writing to php://output",
    "Session cookie without HttpOnly/SameSite (index.php:15, part of F9) — fixed",
    "Array parameters busca[]/login[]/senha[] cause TypeError (index.php:21-22, 72, F15) — fixed",
    "fputcsv without explicit $escape emits Deprecated on PHP 8.4 inside the CSV body (lib.php:130/138, F16) — fixed with the same default values",
    "mediaResposta fetches all rows to sum in PHP instead of SQL aggregation (lib.php:109-115, F17) — fixed with SUM/COUNT",
    "PERF-002 — SELECT * and no pagination in listarChamados (lib.php:80, F18) — reported, not fixed",
    "formatarStatus maps any status other than 1/2 to 'Resolvido' (lib.php:32-33, F19) — reported, deliberately not changed (contracted behaviour)",
    "Dead connect_errno branch on PHP >= 8.1, connection exception reaches the screen (index.php:9-13, F20) — fixed with try/catch",
    "Unanswered critical tickets never flagged by the SLA label (lib.php:56-58, F14) — debatable design observation, low confidence (45), not changed",
    "SEC-005 — no CSRF on the login POST, mentioned only in the deliberate non-changes list (§4 item 8)"
